
- KouChat Android INSTALL

KouChat Android is built with Gradle. README.md contains the full build,
architecture, settings and troubleshooting documentation.

Requirements
------------
- JDK 17 (required by Android Gradle Plugin 8.5)
- Android SDK Platform 36 (compileSdk 36 / targetSdk 36)
- Gradle 8.7, provided by the wrapper (no separate installation)

Prepare
-------
Create local.properties in the project root (this file is not tracked):

  sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/Sdk

Forward slashes work on Windows, macOS and Linux. Android Studio creates this
file automatically when the project is opened.

Gradle runs on the JDK selected by JAVA_HOME (or the java on PATH). The
project deliberately does not hardcode a JDK path in gradle.properties.

Debug build
-----------
  ./gradlew clean test lint assembleDebug        # macOS, Linux, Git Bash
  gradlew.bat clean test lint assembleDebug      # Windows cmd / PowerShell

The installable APK is written to:

  app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

Install it on a connected device with:

  adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

Release build
-------------
  ./gradlew assembleRelease

app/build.gradle does not define a signingConfigs block, so this produces an
UNSIGNED APK:

  app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk

To create a signed release APK, use Android Studio's
"Build > Generate Signed Bundle / APK", add a signingConfigs block to
app/build.gradle, or sign the unsigned APK manually:

  "$ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/34.0.0/apksigner" sign \
    --ks my-release.jks \
    --out app-release-signed.apk \
    app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk

The RELEASE_STORE_FILE, RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD, RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS and
RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD entries in gradle.properties are placeholders. They are
not referenced by any build script, and they must not contain real secrets in
a tracked file.

See https://developer.android.com/studio/publish/app-signing.html for details.
